# drive.press at game.memory 64 with everything the game allocates above 17 MiB (RUSH2049_TEST_HEAP_FLOOR; docs/port/
# MEMORY.md 6): its files, their display lists, textures and vertices, the frame and depth buffers, the sound's
# buffers, all where a physical address would read as a segmented one. The race must be drive's, its picture drawn.
# until: 0x400000:900
# seconds: 90
# expect: state=0x00400000: players 1, windows 1, cars 6, mode 0, track 0
# env: RUSH2049_TEST_HEAP_FLOOR=17
# args: --set game.memory=64 --screenshot-at 1600 --screenshot memhigh.png
# check: tools/port/heap_check.py memhigh.log --memory 64 --floor --short 0
# check: tools/port/synth_shot.py memhigh.png 1
5 A            # the controller pak warning
8 START        # the start prompt
11 A           # the main menu: the race
14 A           # the player screen
17 A           # the mode screen: a single race
20 A           # the track select: track 0
23 A           # the car select; the race starts at about 23.6 s and its countdown runs 3.5 s
27 A 20        # gas for 20 s
32 STICKRIGHT 1.5
36 STICKLEFT 1.5
47 B 3         # the brake
